{"1-6":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H1571","lemma":"גַּם","tr":"gam","gloss":"also","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":769},{"base":"H0369","lemma":"אַ֫יִן","tr":"a·yin","gloss":"nothing","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":788},{"base":"H2416","lemma":"חַי","tr":"chay","gloss":"alive","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":498},{"base":"H4745","lemma":"מִקְרֶה","tr":"miq·reh","gloss":"accident","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H4191","lemma":"מוּת","tr":"mut","gloss":"to die","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":840},{"base":"H8135","lemma":"שִׂנְאָה","tr":"sin·ah","gloss":"hating","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":17},{"base":"H0160","lemma":"אַהֲבָה","tr":"a·ha·vah","gloss":"love","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":38},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":538},{"base":"H3045","lemma":"יָדַע","tr":"ya·da","gloss":"to know","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":945},{"base":"H2076","lemma":"זָבַח","tr":"za·vach","gloss":"to sacrifice","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":134}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":26,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"The dead will not live; the departed spirits will not rise. Therefore You have punished and destroyed them; You have wiped out all memory of them.","from":5},{"book":"ECC","chapter":1,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"There is no remembrance of those who came before, and those yet to come will not be remembered by those who follow after.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":6,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"For there is no mention of You in death; who can praise You from Sheol?","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":88,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"Do You work wonders for the dead? Do departed spirits rise up to praise You? Selah","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":88,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"Will Your wonders be known in the darkness, or Your righteousness in the land of oblivion?","from":5},{"book":"JOB","chapter":14,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"If his sons receive honor, he does not know it; if they are brought low, he is unaware.","from":5},{"book":"HEB","chapter":9,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Just as man is appointed to die once, and after that to face judgment,","from":5},{"book":"DEU","chapter":33,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Surely You love the people; all the holy ones are in Your hand, and they sit down at Your feet; each receives Your words—","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"7-10":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2416","lemma":"חַי","tr":"chay","gloss":"alive","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":498},{"base":"H1892","lemma":"הֶ֫בֶל","tr":"he·vel","gloss":"vanity","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":73},{"base":"H8121","lemma":"שֶׁ֫מֶשׁ","tr":"she·mesh","gloss":"sun","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":134},{"base":"H4639","lemma":"מַעֲשֶׂה","tr":"ma·a·seh","gloss":"deed: work","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":235},{"base":"H2808","lemma":"חֶשְׁבּוֹן","tr":"chesh·bon","gloss":"explanation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H8478","lemma":"תַּחַת","tr":"ta·chat","gloss":"underneath: under","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":505},{"base":"H3528","lemma":"כְּבָר","tr":"ke·var","gloss":"already","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H6001","lemma":"עָמֵל","tr":"a·mel","gloss":"labour(er)","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H0859","lemma":"אַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"you(m.s.)","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1092},{"base":"H2637","lemma":"חָסֵר","tr":"cha·ser","gloss":"to lack","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"COL","chapter":3,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":71,"source":"both","text":"Whatever you do, work at it with your whole being, as for the Lord and not for men,","from":10},{"book":"ROM","chapter":12,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":35,"source":"both","text":"Do not let your zeal subside; keep your spiritual fervor, serving the Lord.","from":10},{"book":"EPH","chapter":5,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":35,"source":"both","text":"redeeming the time, because the days are evil.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":6,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"For there is no mention of You in death; who can praise You from Sheol?","from":10},{"book":"1CO","chapter":9,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"Do you not know that in a race all the runners run, but only one receives the prize? Run in such a way as to take the prize.","from":10},{"book":"ECC","chapter":11,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"Sow your seed in the morning, and do not rest your hands in the evening, for you do not know which will succeed, whether this or that, or if both will equally prosper.","from":10},{"book":"2CH","chapter":31,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"So this is what Hezekiah did throughout Judah. He did what was good and upright and true before the LORD his God.","from":10},{"book":"2CH","chapter":31,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":17,"source":"openbible","text":"He acted with all his heart in every work that he began in the service of the house of God, and in the law and the commandments, in order to seek his God. And so he prospered.","from":10}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"11-18":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2451","lemma":"חׇכְמָה","tr":"chokh·mah","gloss":"wisdom","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":153},{"base":"H4542","lemma":"מִסְכֵּן","tr":"mis·ken","gloss":"poor","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":4},{"base":"H1571","lemma":"גַּם","tr":"gam","gloss":"also","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":769},{"base":"H2450","lemma":"חָכָם","tr":"cha·kham","gloss":"wise","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":138},{"base":"H4685","lemma":"מָצוֹד","tr":"ma·tsod","gloss":"siegework","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H6256","lemma":"עֵת","tr":"et","gloss":"time","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":296},{"base":"H1419","lemma":"גָּדוֹל","tr":"ga·dol","gloss":"great: large","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":526},{"base":"H2896","lemma":"טוֹב","tr":"tov","gloss":"pleasant","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":538},{"base":"H0120","lemma":"אָדָם","tr":"a·dam","gloss":"man","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":550},{"base":"H0270","lemma":"אָחַז","tr":"a·chaz","gloss":"to grasp","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":68}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JER","chapter":9,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":30,"source":"both","text":"This is what the LORD says: “Let not the wise man boast in his wisdom, nor the strong man in his strength, nor the wealthy man in his riches.","from":11},{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":25,"source":"openbible","text":"There is no wisdom, no understanding, no counsel that can prevail against the LORD.","from":11},{"book":"PRO","chapter":21,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":25,"source":"openbible","text":"A horse is prepared for the day of battle, but victory is of the LORD.","from":11},{"book":"LAM","chapter":3,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":21,"source":"openbible","text":"Who has spoken and it came to pass, unless the Lord has ordained it?","from":11},{"book":"LAM","chapter":3,"verse":38,"verseEnd":38,"votes":21,"source":"openbible","text":"Do not both adversity and good come from the mouth of the Most High?","from":11},{"book":"ECC","chapter":3,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"I said in my heart, “God will judge the righteous and the wicked, since there is a time for every activity and every deed.”","from":11},{"book":"JOB","chapter":5,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"He sets the lowly on high, so that mourners are lifted to safety.","from":11},{"book":"JOB","chapter":5,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"They encounter darkness by day and grope at noon as in the night.","from":11}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}